Grace L: Quick heads-up, saw duplicated inference side-effects in sampleapp when a 429 landed at the same time OIDC refresh finished. Tiny repro below.

Grace L: Repro steps:
1) user triggers request U (payload ~80KB)
2) server responds 429
3) SDK immediately schedules a retry (short backoff)
4) auth refresh completes and the original logical op is re-issued -> server processes two separate jobs (no dedupe header)

Hector P: Are we adding any stable op id by default? I don't think so. Server can't dedupe without something stable from the client.

Yuna C: Right now only some examples set headers manually. Parity problem across SDKs.

Grace L: Proposal: introduce a compact header `X-Replay-Token: <uuid>` set once when building the logical request and preserved across retries and refresh flows. Keep streaming ops non-replayable by default. Expose option name: `avoidDuplicateSideEffects` in the client config (boolean).

Hector P: Also add a 'refresh-aware' gating rule: if token refresh is in-flight for this client instance, increase next retry delay by refreshEstimateMs and decrement an in-op retryBudget so we don't do more than N quick retries while refresh is ongoing. Config example: `{ avoidDuplicateSideEffects: true, baseJitterMs: 65, maxQuickRetriesDuringRefresh: 1 }`.

Yuna C: For jitter let's try a different shape: linear payload scaling so small requests stay snappy but large ones spread. Example formula: jitter_ms = baseMs * (1 + payload_kb / 50) * random(0.6..1.4). Works well in our perf runs and is different from sqrt/ln options. Make formula pluggable in sdk-core.

Grace L: Middleware name idea: `replay-guard` (in sdk-core). Responsibilities: generate X-Replay-Token, mark streamed requests as non-replayable unless explicit `replayable: true` set, detect auth refresh state and adjust backoff, and enforce per-op retryBudget. Keep config surface minimal.

Hector P: Add telemetry events so we can measure adoption and regressions: `replay_guard.token_generated`, `replay_guard.retry_blocked_by_refresh`, `replay_guard.replay_sent`, `replay_guard.server_deduped`. That will tell us if servers honor dedupe headers.

Yuna C: For sampleapp onboarding, enable `avoidDuplicateSideEffects` in conservative mode and include a server dedupe snippet with TTL guidance. Example server snippet we can ship: 
```
const seen = new Map();
app.post('/v1/generate', (req, res) => {
  const token = req.get('X-Replay-Token');
  if (token && seen.has(token)) return res.status(200).json({ duplicate: true });
  if (token) seen.set(token, Date.now());
  // normal processing...
});
// TTL cleanup job: remove tokens older than min(max(1000, estimatedProcessingMs * 2), 30000) ms
```

Grace L: Also add an e2e test: simulate 429 + refresh taking 350ms; ensure only one accepted when X-Replay-Token present. Test should exercise streaming-no-replay path too.

Hector P: Edge case: if server doesn't support header, we still reduce duplicates by gating retries during refresh and having the retryBudget small. Good fallback.

devex-bot: (automated) Created DEVTICKET-812: "replay-guard middleware + X-Replay-Token + linear payload jitter + refresh-aware retryBudget + onboarding conservative mode + e2e tests"

Yuna C: I'll draft the Node implementation and sampleapp changes, Hector can map to Go and Java SDKs for parity, Grace will own the core spec and telemetry names. Add to SDK sync agenda. :calendar:
